  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Water Resource Management Programme for the Lake Victoria Basin with High Priority Investments</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the programme is to improve water quality and availability through strategic and sustainable management of the Lake Victoria Basin via regional measures of integrated water resource management (IWRM). In addition to an environmentally sound and economically viable management of the water resources, the set of measures will have a positive effect on the enhancement of regional economic integration, to the preservation of Biodiversity and to prevention of conflicts. To achieve the objective an integrated, programmatic regional approach will be established with the following specific objectives:1)Specific Objective 1: LVBC Secretariat performs its function of strategic regional water resource management; 2)Specific Objective 2: Effluents into the Lake Victoria are reduced through targeted infrastructure investments in waste water and solid waste management.</narrative>
  </description>
